WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.549
If you walked away from Jurassic World: Fallen
Kingdom with a bit of whiplash, don't be alarmed.

00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:08.621
The sequel easily feels like three different
movies crammed into one, and each act could

00:00:08.621 --> 00:00:12.420
presents its own unique horrors before the
big finish brings everything together and

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.280
swiftly smashes it all to bits.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.499
Taking place three years after the events
of Jurassic World, it takes some suspension

00:00:18.499 --> 00:00:23.109
of disbelief to get our old friends Owen and
Claire back to Isla Nublar, and the visit

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:25.520
goes just about as smoothly as one might expect.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.880
That's just the start of their troubles, too,
as they face even bigger monsters on the mainland.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.040
Let's take a look at what exactly happens
there at the tail end of Jurassic World: Fallen

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.280
Kingdom, and tie together all of the film's
plot threads.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.180
A bedside betrayal

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:43.520
The introduction of deep-pocketed dino philanthropist
Benjamin Lockwood explains how Hammond could

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.480
afford the original, outrageously expensive
Jurassic Park.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.220
He's also a friendly face for the new Isla
Nublar expedition; one that can convince people

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.860
to join in, especially those who were involved
with the previous massacre.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:59.059
Lockwood plays on Claire's desire to save
these dinosaurs from certain extinction by

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:03.149
the island's erupting volcano, and she in
turn plays on Owen's personal connection to

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:04.160
the raptor Blue.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.619
Lockwood may have been sincere about saving
the dinosaurs, but his smarmy assistant Eli

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:13.040
Mills is much too greedy to simply rehouse
these animals on some tranquil island.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.540
Instead, he's ready to round up whatever creatures
he can to auction them off to the highest

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.040
bidder.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:23.240
At the same time, he's also working with mad
geneticist Dr. Wu to create an even more lethal

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.140
and valuable — weapon of war called the
indoraptor.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.700
This thing is a hybrid of the indominus rex
and the velociraptor, and even more menacing

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.980
than its parent species.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.580
Once Mills' true intentions are discovered
by Lockwood, he decides to smother his longtime

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:41.270
benefactor to death and go about the business
of turning his late boss' passion project

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.090
into a personal fortune anyway.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.040
What a guy.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.960
A particular taste

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.180
Mills has no trouble rounding up buyers for
his new menagerie of monsters.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.460
Blue was the VIP target Claire and Owen were
recruited to save, but it wasn't a charity

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.300
mission at all.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.320
Owen's behavior research with Blue is important,
because the indoraptor Wu has created won't

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.200
work as-is.

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:05.140
He wants to make another one that grows up
with Blue, so that it can pick up her trained

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.590
traits of empathy and emotional intelligence.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.440
The prototype that's displayed and unwisely
auctioned off by Mills is a merciless killing

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.560
machine that won't be any good to a squadron
of soldiers running with it.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.280
Owen and Claire could easily walk away from
the fray at Lockwood's estate once they get

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.540
the pachycephalosaurus to break them out.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:26.180
But instead Owen decides to hang around long
enough to ensure Wu's gene-spliced monstrosity

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.760
won't ever leave the manor alive.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.220
That's when all hell breaks loose at the Lockwood
auction.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.360
Twisted family tree

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.980
Poor Maisie spends her whole life being cared
for by the ailing, secretive man she knows

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:41.620
as her grandpa, but he refuses to even show
her a photo of the mother she supposedly lost

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:42.880
to land her in his care.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.220
After he's executed by Mills, she discovers
that she's a clone of his late daughter, and

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.660
not actually his granddaughter.

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:52.980
In other words, it's not just dinosaur DNA
that's creating new life in this story; human

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.580
beings are also ripe for the cloning process
now.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.320
Blue's on the move

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:01.980
As Mill's auction starts to fall apart, most
of the dinosaurs are still locked up in the

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.380
lower containment area.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:07.780
That'd be all well and good for everyone on
site, except that the fracas eventually reaches

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:12.049
the lower levels, when Wu demands that Zia
and Franklin steal Blue's blood so he can

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:14.780
save it for the next horror hybrid he decides
to create.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.750
The two refuse and let Blue loose on the lab
guards.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:22.140
That saves them and the raptor eventually
rescues Owen, Claire and Maisie above from

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.120
the indoraptor.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.940
But her escape causes a fire blast and a toxic
chemical leak that threatens to kill all of

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.680
the rescued dinos in cages.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.140
Although she's spent years trying to save
these exact creatures, Claire chooses not

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.820
to let them out because it's too dangerous
to have them wandering around civilized society.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.840
But in a twist, Maisie steps up to let them
loose anyway.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.840
She now knows just how much she has in common
with these engineered creatures.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.769
Outside, Owen asks Blue to stick with him,
but she decides to check out what the rest

00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:50.200
of the world has to offer instead.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.080
No more hybrids?

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.370
In the madness, Mills' only concern seems
to be to preserve the indominus rex bone they

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:02.020
fished out from the mosasaurus tank because
of how valuable it'll be to military geneticists.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:06.400
However, his luck ultimately runs out, and
the T-rex eventually stomps the sample to

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.560
pieces, which means the indominus rex is gone…
but perhaps not forever?

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.220
The hybrid story could indeed continue, as
the indoraptor's skeleton is down below Isla

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:15.720
Nublar.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:20.040
For now, though, everyone who was crazy enough
to do that initial dive is dead, so we'll

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:24.730
have to wait and see if Jurassic World 3 would
even bother to bring back the hybrid concept

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.440
when they've got so much else to work with.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.640
Welcome to Jurassic World

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.700
Ian Malcolm warned everyone not to save the
dinosaurs from the volcano at Isla Nublar.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.140
This is the same guy who once scolded the
Jurassic Park team by saying:

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.320
"Your scientists were so preoccupied with
whether or not they could, they didn't stop

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:40.980
to think if they should!"

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:45.020
And in the end, he ends up explaining to the
nation that humans now have to find a way

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:49.560
to adapt to and co-exist with these creatures,
lest they be wiped out by them.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:53.280
For good measure, we see that scientists have
collected plenty of vials of DNA to ensure

00:04:53.280 --> 00:05:00.220
the survival of the species, so it's not just
up to the group from Maisie's arc to repopulate

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.180
It's legitimately Jurassic World now

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.720
Humans are now on the defensive, and dinosaurs
are ready to inherit the Earth once more—

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.940
as we see in the post-credits scene, which
depicts pteranodons circling

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.340
the Eiffel Tower replica in Las Vegas.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:13.860
Remember the giant Mosasaurus?

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.700
It's now on the loose, preying
on anything it can find throughout the ocean...

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:22.220
Even worse, the prehistoric beings seem open
to inviting the rest of modern nature to rejoin

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:26.890
the wild kingdom, as the T-rex breaks down
a lion's cage and exchanges a few friendly

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:29.360
roars with the erstwhile king of the jungle.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:33.920
If and when Jurassic World 3 happens, it sounds
like it's going to live up to its namesake

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.500
Thanks for watching!

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.330
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.580
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

